MambaManager.find_longest_cache_hit accepts drop_eagle_block and never reads it,
so an MTP/EAGLE prefix-cache hit can resume from a recurrent-state snapshot taken
over draft tokens that verification later rejected. Result is wrong output with no
error (vllm#48375 / vllm#43559). The corrupted state is hash-reachable, so every
later request sharing that prefix restores from it.

Upstream: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48375 (still open, needs rebase)

Why lowering max_length rather than max_num_blocks -= 1:
the PR lowers the coarse search ceiling, but with --prefix-match-unit 16 the
fine-grained branch above it runs instead and returns early. Reducing max_length
bounds both: max_num_partial_units = min(max_length // hash_block_size, ...) and
max_num_blocks = max_length // block_size. Arithmetically identical for the coarse
case ((x - b) // b == x // b - 1). Same approach as the 4x sm_80 production
deployment reported in the PR thread.

Apply (from the venv's site-packages, so paths line up):

    cd .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages
    patch -p1 --dry-run < ../../../../experiments/vllm-48375-mamba-drop-eagle-block.patch
    patch -p1 < ../../../../experiments/vllm-48375-mamba-drop-eagle-block.patch

Verify it took:

    grep -n "drop_eagle_block" vllm/v1/core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py

There should now be a hit in the MambaManager body (around line 1423), not only in
the signature at line 1400.

PERSISTENCE WARNING: this edits the installed package. `uv sync`, a reinstall, or a
vLLM upgrade will silently drop it and re-introduce the silent-corruption bug. If
you turn on --enable-prefix-caching, re-run the grep above after any dependency
change.

--- a/vllm/v1/core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py
@@ -1422,4 +1422,10 @@
         block_size = kv_cache_spec.block_size
+        if drop_eagle_block:
+            # An EAGLE/MTP cache hit must not reuse the final matched block: its
+            # recurrent-state snapshot may have been taken over draft positions
+            # that verification later rejected. Lowering max_length bounds both
+            # the fine-grained and coarse searches below (vllm#48375, #43559).
+            max_length = max(0, max_length - block_size)
         if alignment_tokens < block_size and block_size % alignment_tokens == 0:
             # list or lazy BlobBlockHashes view
             assert isinstance(block_hashes, Sequence)
